			"Message": "chore(Mist): Update Documentation/Rust submodule pointer\n\nAdvance the `Documentation/Rust` submodule from `84bb64e0` to `6b341399`, picking up one new commit:\n  - `3ce319f` docs(Mist): Replace ASCII architecture diagram with Mermaid graph\n\nThis non-functional update keeps the checked-out documentation in sync with the Mist repository's latest README revision.",
			"SHA": "fceec3419827a9d568ad4ef06431b8e98f13b466"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T04:19:38Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				20,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mist): Replace ASCII architecture diagram with Mermaid graph\n\nThe static ASCII art in `README.md` depicting Mist's DNS architecture was difficult to maintain and update. Replace it with a proper Mermaid `graph LR` diagram that uses semantic node styling and labels each module by its source file (Server.rs, Zone.rs, ForwardSecurity.rs, Resolver.rs, WebSocket.rs).\n\nThe new diagram adds explicit color-coded CSS classes for each subsystem (Mist, zone, forward allowlist, consumers, external), structures the layout into three labelled subgraphs (Land Components, Mist Local DNS Server, External), and uses directed edges to show the startup and query flow among Mountain, Cocoon, Air, and Mist. Component names now include emoji icons (🌫️, ⛰️, 🦋, 🪁, ☁️) for visual clarity.\n\nThis improves long-term maintainability of the documentation and makes the architecture immediately scannable for new contributors.",
			"SHA": "3ce319f67e175b46565e34ee628fe1cb512e9a5f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T00:58:28Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				20,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Mist): Update documentation submodule and refine test formatting\n\nUpdate the `Documentation/Rust` submodule to initialize the root `README.md` for the Mist component, establishing the documentation infrastructure. Simultaneously, remove an unnecessary blank line in the test module within `Source/ForwardSecurity.rs` to align with Rust formatting conventions.\n\nThese changes ensure the component documentation structure is in place and the codebase maintains consistent whitespace hygiene.",
			"SHA": "b5ada5fea23162631cd0e5b1e8fe445caa943977"
		},
